# Admin nav sidebar addition

In your `AdminLayout` (likely `client/src/components/admin/AdminLayout.tsx` or
`client/src/pages/admin/layout.tsx` — wherever the admin sidebar lives), add
a new nav item alongside the existing admin pages (users, companies, billing,
email-templates, etc.):

```tsx
import { Megaphone } from "lucide-react";  // or any icon you prefer

// Inside your nav items array:
{
  label: "Lead Gen",
  href: "/admin/lead-gen",
  icon: Megaphone,
  // If your pattern uses a children/submenu array:
  children: [
    { label: "Overview", href: "/admin/lead-gen" },
    { label: "Leads", href: "/admin/lead-gen/leads" },
    { label: "Campaigns", href: "/admin/lead-gen/campaigns" },
    { label: "Templates", href: "/admin/lead-gen/templates" },
    { label: "Settings", href: "/admin/lead-gen/settings" },
  ],
},
```

If the sidebar is hand-rolled (just a list of `<Link>`s), just add:

```tsx
<Link href="/admin/lead-gen" className="...">
  <Megaphone className="h-4 w-4" />
  Lead Gen
</Link>
```
